<title>BULGARIA: Yield falls on Bulgaria 3-mth discount T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Bulgaria 3-mth discount T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield to maturity on Bulgaria's Finance ministry three-month discount T-bills fell to 8.08 percent at Monday's auction from 8.32 percent a week earlier, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with a par value of nine billion levs and no minimum acceptable price set in advance and was 31.16 percent sold.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		 BG3035897001</p>
<p> Maturity		     three months</p>
<p> Par value		    9,000 million levs</p>
<p> Auction date		 May 26</p>
<p> Issue date		   May 28</p>
<p> Maturity date		August 27</p>
<p> Bids received		2,804.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	  92.52 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		2,804.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	 92.52 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity    8.08 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
